title: Seventeen Per Cent
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and time >= 23 and time <= 25 and interest_rate < 17 and mlr17_seen = 0 and inflation >= 12
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: mlr17_seen = 1
face-image: img/events/bank_1983.jpg

= Seventeen Per Cent

The money supply is growing far faster than our target, and inflation is [+ inflation_2 +]%. The Bank of England recommends raising Bank Rate to an unprecedented 17%.

- @raise: Do it.
- @refuse: Refuse. The recession is bad enough.

@raise
on-arrival: interest_rate = 17; inflation -= 1; sterling += 4; c1_con -= 2; c2_con -= 1; dry_dissent -= 4; wet_dissent += 4
achievement: seventeen

Bank Rate goes to 17%, the highest in its history. Mortgage rates follow, and industry howls.

@refuse
on-arrival: inflation += 1; economic_liberalism -= 2; dry_dissent += 6; wet_dissent -= 3

We hold rates where they are. The markets conclude the government's monetarism has limits.
